mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Radio Crepuscular 99.5 FM — Backend API\n\nBackend for the community radio station Radio Crepuscular 99.5 FM (Barquisimeto, Lara, Venezuela). It stores the station's news articles and its weekly program schedule.\n\n## Authentication and identity\n\n- `listNews`, `getNews` and `listSchedule` are public queries: any caller, including anonymous visitors, can read them.\n- `createNews`, `updateNews` and `deleteNews` require a signed-in caller with at least the `#user` role. An anonymous or unregistered caller receives a trap: `Unauthorized: Only signed-in staff can publish news` (or the matching message for edit/delete).\n- Registration happens only when a caller signs in through the app's own frontend. A principal that never signed in through the frontend is unregistered even if it belongs to the station owner. The first caller to invoke `_initialize_access_control` becomes the admin; later callers become regular users.\n- The frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin`. An agent already holding the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n- A direct API caller must call `_initialize_access_control` once as a signed-in caller before any role-guarded call.\n\n## Methods\n\n### `listNews() : async [NewsItem]` (query)\nReturns all news articles, newest first by `publishedAt`. Public.\n\n### `getNews(id : nat) : async ?NewsItem` (query)\nReturns one article by id, or `null` if it does not exist. Public.\n\n### `createNews(title : text, body : text) : async NewsItem`\nCreates an article authored by the caller. Requires a signed-in `#user`. Returns the created item.\n\n### `updateNews(id : nat, title : text, body : text) : async Result<NewsItem, NewsError>`\nUpdates an article. Requires a signed-in `#user` and the caller must be the article's original author. Returns `#ok(item)` on success, `#err(#notFound(id))` if the id does not exist, or `#err(#notAuthor(id))` if the caller is not the author.\n\n### `deleteNews(id : nat) : async Result<(), NewsError>`\nDeletes an article. Requires a signed-in `#user` and the caller must be the article's original author. Returns `#ok(())`, `#err(#notFound(id))`, or `#err(#notAuthor(id))`.\n\n### `listSchedule() : async [ProgramSlot]` (query)\nReturns the weekly program schedule, ordered Monday-first by weekday and then by start time. Public.\n\n## Types\n\n- `NewsItem = { id : nat; title : text; body : text; publishedAt : int; author : principal }`\n- `NewsError = { #notFound : nat; #notAuthor : nat }`\n- `ProgramSlot = { weekday : Weekday; startTime : text; endTime : text; name : text; description : text }`\n- `Weekday = { #monday; #tuesday; #wednesday; #thursday; #friday; #saturday; #sunday }`\n\n## Units and encoding\n\n- `publishedAt` is a timestamp in **nanoseconds** since the Unix epoch (signed 64-bit integer). Divide by 1,000,000,000 for seconds.\n- `startTime` and `endTime` are zero-padded 24-hour `\"HH:MM\"` text, so plain text comparison orders them correctly.\n- `id` values are non-negative integers assigned sequentially by the backend.\n- `author` is the principal of the staff member who created the article.\n\n## Lifecycle, polling and retry safety\n\n- All reads are `query` calls and never mutate state.\n- `createNews` is not idempotent: each call creates a new article with a new id. Retrying after a timeout may create a duplicate.\n- `updateNews` and `deleteNews` are idempotent in effect: repeating an update with the same values leaves the same result, and repeating a delete returns `#err(#notFound(id))` after the first success.\n- `deleteNews` is destructive and cannot be undone.\n\n## Errors and gotchas\n\n- Authorization failures on `createNews`/`updateNews`/`deleteNews` are traps, not `Result` errors; the frontend sees an opaque reject with the message above.\n- Ownership is enforced per article: a signed-in staff member cannot edit or delete another author's article.\n- `getNews` returns `null` for a missing id rather than trapping."
  };
};
